<title>JAPAN: TABLE-Japan June housing starts down 11.6 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Japan June housing starts down 11.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's housing starts slipped 11.6 percent in June from a year earlier to 120,842 units, falling for the sixth consecutive month on a year-on-year basis, the Construction Ministry said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The ministry also released data for the April-to-June period which showed housing starts for the period had fallen 10.2 percent from the same period a year ago to 370,638 units.</p>
<p>The following is the breakdown of June housing starts.</p>
<p>			June starts	     yr/yr pct change</p>
<p> Private homes	    42,549		     - 21.7</p>
<p> Rental homes	     45,708		     - 12.0</p>
<p> Employee housing	  2,236		     +  5.1</p>
<p> Housing built for sale 30,349		     +  7.4</p>
<p>  Condominiums	    17,335		     + 13.1</p>
<p> Total		     120,842		     - 11.6</p>
</text>
